docs/arnold/m5b-plugin-relocation-map.md:9:This map records the settled source-to-target mappings for the four policy domains moving into the Megaplan plugin under `arnold/pipelines/megaplan/` during M5b: **execute**, **review**, **orchestration**, and **audits**.
docs/arnold/m5b-plugin-relocation-map.md:25:| **Cross-domain Dependencies** | Depends on `orchestration.evaluation`, `orchestration.execution_evidence`, and `audits.quality_gates` |
docs/arnold/m5b-plugin-relocation-map.md:35:| **Reason** | Megaplan-specific phase-result transport, progress emission, evaluation, gate signals, completion contracts, iteration pressure, and recovery policy. Deep imports from `megaplan.schemas`, `megaplan.store`, `megaplan.types`. No reusable Arnold substrate. |
docs/arnold/m5b-plugin-relocation-map.md:36:| **Key Vocabulary** | `PhaseResult`, `ExitKind`, `ProgressContext`, `ProgressEvent`, `gate_signals`, `recovery_policy`, `iteration_pressure` |
