docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:5:In this report, "native" means more than "the workflow is authored in Python." It means the workflow's product semantics are visible in the Python control flow itself: loops are loops, gates are branches, tiebreakers are subworkflows, review rework is an explicit cycle, human intervention is a suspension point, and task execution fanout is not hidden behind a single opaque handler call.
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:11:- a prep clarification gate;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:12:- adaptive critique evaluation with retry;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:13:- parallel critique lenses with fan-in;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:14:- a bounded critique/gate/revise loop with severity-aware termination;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:16:- finalize fallback routes;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:18:- execute/review/rework loops;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:41:- steps are `Step(...)` objects with ids such as `prep`, `plan`, `critique`, `gate`, `revise`, `tiebreaker_run`, `tiebreaker_decide`, `finalize`, `execute`, `review`, `halt`, and `override`;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:44:- a few policy slots are attached, such as loop metadata on `revise` and `tiebreaker_decide`, suspension routes on `gate` and `review`, and control transition slots on `gate`, `review`, and `tiebreaker_decide`.
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:49:prep -> plan -> critique -> gate
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:50:                          |-- proceed -> finalize -> execute -> review -> halt
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:51:                          |-- iterate -> revise -> critique
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:52:                          |-- tiebreaker -> tiebreaker_run -> tiebreaker_decide -> critique
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:71:- `planned -> critique -> critiqued`;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:72:- `critiqued -> gate/revise/tiebreaker/override`;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:73:- `gated -> finalize`;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:74:- `finalized -> execute`;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:75:- `executed -> review -> done`;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:76:- `blocked -> override force-proceed -> finalized`;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:78:- `tiebreaker_ready -> tiebreaker-decide -> critiqued`.
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:80:It also has robustness overrides. For example, `bare` allows `planned -> finalize`, and `light` bypasses the full review path by emptying `STATE_EXECUTED` transitions (`arnold_pipelines/megaplan/_core/workflow_data.py:95`).
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:92:  -> critique
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:93:  -> gate
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:94:  -> revise/gate loop until acceptable
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:95:  -> finalize
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:97:  -> review
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:106:The important product decision is the prep clarification gate. `_apply_prep_clarify_gate()` checks prep output for blocking open questions. If blocking questions exist, the plan enters `STATE_AWAITING_HUMAN_VERIFY`; otherwise it enters `STATE_PREPPED` (`arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/plan.py:21`, `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/plan.py:209`).
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:123:### Critique
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:125:Critique judges the plan before execution. It may:
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:128:- run adaptive critique evaluator logic;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:129:- select a subset of critique lenses;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:131:- fan out parallel critique workers over selected checks;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:132:- fall back to sequential critique if parallel execution fails;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:133:- write scratch and structured critique artifacts.
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:135:The retry and fanout are top-level product structure hidden in `handle_critique()` (`arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/critique.py:279`). The evaluator retry loop starts around `_MAX_EVAL_ATTEMPTS = 2` (`arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/critique.py:384`). Parallel critique dispatch is at `run_parallel_critique(...)` (`arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/critique.py:710`).
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:137:In native form, critique is a small subworkflow:
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:141:    return SkipCritique()
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:143:selection = await retry(critique_evaluator, attempts=2)
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:144:findings = await parallel_map(selection.active_checks, run_critique_lens)
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:145:critique_payload = await merge_critique(findings)
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:150:Gate is the central plan-quality decision. It builds signals, invokes a gate worker, normalizes or recovers the worker response, validates flag resolution, reprompts once when unresolved blocking flags remain, applies high-complexity unverifiable-check backstops, records debt on accepted tradeoffs, and routes to proceed, iterate, tiebreaker, blocked, abort, or override.
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:154:- `_apply_gate_outcome()` starts at `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/gate.py:494`;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:155:- `handle_gate()` starts at `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/gate.py:792`;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:156:- high-complexity unverifiable checks are applied after the worker result (`arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/gate.py:879`);
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:157:- unresolved blocking flags trigger a gate reprompt (`arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/gate.py:911`);
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:158:- the second pass is merged and can still downgrade to iterate (`arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/gate.py:984`).
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:160:Gate is where the critique/gate/revise loop is controlled. At a cap or no-progress threshold, critical unresolved flags lead to `STATE_BLOCKED`, while cosmetic-only unresolved work can force-proceed to `STATE_GATED`. That termination policy is product topology, not incidental parsing logic.
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:164:Revise updates the plan based on gate feedback. It is the body of the critique loop. `handle_revise()` starts at `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/critique.py:1055`.
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:166:The current top-level graph already marks `revise` with a bounded loop policy (`arnold_pipelines/megaplan/workflows/planning.py:191`), but the branch of whether to go back through critique, gate, or terminate is still distributed across handler state mutations and workflow state logic.
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:170:Tiebreaker handles split or ambiguous gate judgments. It has two handler phases:
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:178:gate says TIEBREAKER
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:179:  -> researcher and challenger investigate rival interpretations
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:181:  -> pick goes back into revise/critique, escalate waits for human, replan restarts planning
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:188:Finalize turns a gated plan into executable tasks, sense checks, watch items, user actions, validation metadata, and baseline/test-selection details. `handle_finalize()` starts at `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/finalize.py:1661`.
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:190:One topology-relevant branch is error fallback: `FinalizeBaselineSelectionError` can route back to revise (`arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/finalize.py:64`, `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/finalize.py:1713`).
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:194:Execute runs the finalized task plan. `handle_execute()` starts at `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/execute.py:134`.
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:201:- forces fresh sessions for review rework or blocked retries;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:202:- tracks blocked tasks and quality-gate failures;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:203:- writes stub reviews when review is skipped;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:204:- transitions directly to done or human verification for no-review robustness levels.
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:210:Review judges the completed work. `handle_review()` starts at `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/review.py:1297`.
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:218:- retry review on infrastructure failure;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:219:- run parallel review checks for extreme robustness;
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:223:The main outcome state machine is `_resolve_review_outcome()` (`arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/review.py:722`). Parallel review is dispatched through `run_parallel_review(...)` (`arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/review.py:1466`).
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:225:### Override and human gates
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:239:| `critique` | `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/critique.py:279` | Bare skip, adaptive evaluator, evaluator retry, active-lens selection, parallel critique fanout, sequential fallback. | Yes. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:240:| Critique evaluator retry | `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/critique.py:384` | One initial evaluator attempt plus one retry, with raw-output recovery. | Yes, as retry policy on a sub-step. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:241:| Parallel critique | `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/critique.py:710` | Multiple checks run concurrently and merge. | Yes, as parallel map/fan-in. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:242:| `gate` | `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/gate.py:792` | Signal build, worker call, validation, retry/reprompt, recommendation recovery, debt recording, route selection. | Yes. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:243:| Gate outcome routing | `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/gate.py:494` | Proceed/iterate/tiebreaker/escalate/blocked decisions plus cap/no-progress termination. | Yes, as a decision node plus loop policy. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:244:| Gate reprompt | `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/gate.py:911` | Re-run gate worker once when blocking unresolved flags remain. | Yes, as retry/repair edge. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:245:| Gate high-complexity backstop | `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/gate.py:879` | PROCEED is auto-downgraded to ITERATE if high-complexity unverifiable checks exist. | Yes, as post-gate validation branch. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:246:| Gate debt recording | `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/gate.py:78` | Accepted tradeoffs/unresolved concerns become debt entries on PROCEED. | Partial, as an effect on the proceed edge. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:247:| `revise` | `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/critique.py:1055` | Updates plan and re-enters critique/gate loop. | Partial; top-level loop already exists, but routing should be clearer. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:248:| Tiebreaker validation | `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/critique.py:1194` | Validates tiebreaker eligibility and can reprompt/route. | Yes, as explicit tiebreaker gate. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:251:| `finalize` | `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/finalize.py:1661` | Baseline-selection failure fallback to revise. | Yes, as error edge. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:252:| `execute` | `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/execute.py:134` | Batch vs auto-loop, user/destructive gates, blocked retry, fresh sessions, no-review terminal routing. | Yes. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:255:| `review` | `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/review.py:1297` | Review mode selection, parallel review, outcome state machine, rework cap, human verification. | Yes. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:256:| Review outcome | `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/review.py:722` | Approved/needs-rework/blocked routing, cap behavior, force-proceed vs blocked. | Yes, as decision plus loop. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:257:| Parallel review | `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/handlers/review.py:1466` | Extreme robustness fanout and merge. | Yes. |
