docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:777:- review human suspension and control transitions (`arnold_pipelines/megaplan/workflows/planning.py:269`).
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md:785:Megaplan does not know all critique checks, review checks, task batches, or tiebreaker shape as static literal branches at import time. The current native `parallel()` helper requires a literal list/tuple of `@phase` callables (`arnold/pipeline/native/decorators.py:177`). That works for deliberation-style fixed panels; it is not enough for Megaplan's runtime lists.
