docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave2/w2-06-agent-tool-model-surface.txt:7:**1. Agent/tool/model dispatch contract.** `arnold.agent` is a large existing neutral package (adapters for Codex/DeepSeek/Shannon, tools for browser/terminal/vision/MCP/session/search, providers, sandbox wrappers, budget/token tracking, approval gates). M3 builds `arnold.execution` and M4 says product "may depend on" `arnold.agent` — but **no milestone defines the capability/effect dispatch seam between the runtime and the agent**. Without it, M4 discovers that the runner cannot invoke a model, route through OpenRouter, enforce budget caps, sandbox a terminal call, or require approval without importing product policy. **Gap:** every tool in `arnold/agent/tools/` (browser, terminal, vision, MCP, session, file_ops, web, sandbox) is a capability that must be registered against a neutral runtime dispatch contract. The plan says "capability checks" in M3 but never names the agent-tool surface.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave2/w2-06-agent-tool-model-surface.txt:9:**2. Live smoke testing surface.** M4 done criteria #6 says "At least one live-backed smoke run succeeds" — but no milestone defines what "live" means (real API calls? real model inference? real file system?). The fake-backend tests in M3 are deterministic, but the jump from fake to live carries risks around credential injection, rate limiting, budget exhaustion, tool side-effects, and idempotency of real external calls. No smoke gate exists between M3 fake-run and M4 live-backed.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave2/w2-06-agent-tool-model-surface.txt:21:| `arnold/kernel/human.py` vs `suspension.py` | **Leaked.** Human gates are product; suspension is kernel. M1 touchpoints blur this. | Product policy leaks into neutral kernel. |
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave2/w2-06-agent-tool-model-surface.txt:40:| **M4** | Reduce M2 pattern set: defer `panel`/`tournament`/`merge` to M4 as product compositions. Add committed `legacy-surface-inventory.md`. Add on-disk state migration plan. Add live-smoke gate after fake-backend parity. |
