docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-03-straggler-risk.txt:604:- Lower branch, loop, fanout, retry, human gate, and subpipeline shapes to manifest scopes and `reentry_id`s.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-03-straggler-risk.txt:625:- Runtime branching uses `branch`, `loop`, `fanout`, `retry`, `subpipeline`, and `human_gate`, not Python `if`/`while` over runtime refs.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-03-straggler-risk.txt:650:2. Pattern lowering tests cover branch, loop, fanout, retry, human gate, subpipeline, merge, and external call.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-03-straggler-risk.txt:685:The briefs already absorbed two review waves, so I’m checking less for “missing entire phase” and more for places where the final purge can pass while debris remains outside the named manifests and package paths.
