docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-03-straggler-risk.txt:1657:briefs/epic-pipeline-unification/m5-cal.md:5:> **What this milestone is.** Today routing is a TOML read: a profile expansion produces `metadata["tier_models"]` (`profiles/__init__.py:34,119–138`), a finalize step adjudicates an integer `complexity` in 1..5 against a rubric (`handlers/finalize.py:264–268`, defaulting out-of-range to tier 4, `:582–586`), and `batch.py:79–98` resolves `tier_models.execute.<tier>` → agent/model with no record read back. The (complexity, model, verdict, cost) receipts that DO get written (`_pipeline/receipt.py:105–110`, `cost.py:100–118` `COST_RECORDED`) are **never read back** to inform the next route (SYNTHESIS UU#10). M5-cal makes the Calibration Ledger the authority: a content-hashed, append-only record of **CapabilityClaims + adjudicated outcomes**, with the three primitives the soul-lens demands — **DECAY/CHURN**, **EXPLORATION BUDGET**, **TAINT-AWARE AGGREGATION** — so that the 1–5 score and `tier_models` become **projections of the Ledger** and **routing becomes a query, not a TOML read**.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-03-straggler-risk.txt:1658:briefs/epic-pipeline-unification/m5-cal.md:15:1. **CapabilityClaim record + write path into the one Ledger.** New record `CapabilityClaim{task_signature (typed, domain-tagged), predicted_tier:int, routed_model:ModelIdentity, verifier_identity, verifier_tier, outcome:EvaluandRef, cost, counterfactual_tag, taint_class, recorded_at}`. **The `outcome:EvaluandRef` references M5-eval's FULL attributable, taint-bearing Evaluand record `{piece-version, judge-version, rubric-version, input-set-hash, score, provenance, taint, recorded_at}` (m5-eval.md Outcome #2 / Scope #2 / Done #2) — NOT M4's thinner `{judge-version, rubric-version, input-set-hash, score}` scaffold.** This is the single taint source: M5-cal's taint-aware aggregation (Scope #6) reads the `taint` field that ONLY the M5-eval attributable record carries (the M4 scaffold has no taint field). The outcome is **never a bare float** — enforced by a type assertion + grep gate. Write on every adjudicated dispatch via the M4 `EventSink.emit` one-log path (m4 §7, R5), keyed by the R7 hash-pinned `model_identity` seeded into `COST_RECORDED` at M1 (`cost.py:100–118`). New module `megaplan/calibration/ledger.py`.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-03-straggler-risk.txt:1660:briefs/epic-pipeline-unification/m5-cal.md:73:- `megaplan/observability/cost.py:23,71–118` — R7 `model_identity` source (seeded M1); the sensors (prefix-cache-hit-rate, monoculture index) feeding the gated experiments; the NEW path stops reading the substring `_classify_vendor` once the Ledger is the source (report-only here; the OLD read stays live, retired with R5 at M6 per m4 §7).
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-03-straggler-risk.txt:1661:briefs/epic-pipeline-unification/m5-cal.md:74:- `megaplan/handlers/finalize.py:264–268,559–608` — tier adjudication wrap site (projection parity; query suggestion).
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-03-straggler-risk.txt:1689:briefs/epic-pipeline-unification/m4-services-spine.md:28:6. **The RecoveryPolicy spine (carried + the Capacity-Lease fold).** **(a) `RecoveryPolicy.classify`** extracts auto.py's brain: `ExitKind` (`phase_result.py:19` — success/blocked_by_quality/blocked_by_prereq/timeout/context_exhausted/internal_error/external_error), `_is_retryable_external_error` (`auto.py:196`), `EXTERNAL_RETRYABLE_PHASES/_LAYERS` (`:79,97`), the three retry loops with separate caps (context-exhaustion `~:1777`, transient `~:1832`, blocked-task `DEFAULT_MAX_BLOCKED_RETRIES=1` `:110,2406`). Auto.py's loops become bindings over ONE injected policy. **`halt(kind)`/`escalate` stay target-agnostic** (no `STATE_*` — M5c owns the control vocabulary). **(b) ONE live budget authority + Capacity-Lease fold.** Three uncoordinated counters reconcile through it: `CostTracker` cap reading only `state["meta"]["total_cost_usd"]` (`_pipeline/runtime.py:58,71`), the loop time budget (`loop/engine.py:31,81`), the dispatch attribution journal. Home it in the cross-process broker beside `key_pool.py` (in-process today: `threading.Lock` `:69`, module-global `_pool` `:197`, `time.monotonic` cooldowns `:160,175,187` not cross-process-comparable). **The M3 Capacity-Lease (the `fcntl.flock`'d ledger, fencing tokens) is the fold point:** each fan-out shard's spend folds into the single tree budget through the Lease, so the aggregate is bounded (UU#8 fork-bomb defense — a recursive AI-emitted graph cannot pass N local caps while the tree is unbounded). Cooldowns move to wall-clock `time.time()` in the shared ledger; reserve a per-tenant sub-budget field. **In-process fallback byte-identical when no shared ledger.** **(c) Composition-observability contract** the driver emits by default (step boundary, decision+rationale, retry+class, budget delta, piece identity); **re-home `introspect/doctor/trace/cost`** (`observability/{introspect,doctor,trace,cost}.py`, all hardwired to `read_events` + `find_plan_dir`) onto it so a non-plan composition is observable without a `plan_dir`.
