docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-02-technical-abstractions.txt:371:The reviewer should be able to see a committed manifest v1 contract, golden/parity fixtures, conformance gates, and a quarry map that says exactly what is preserved or rejected from `native-python-pipelines` and adjacent branches.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-02-technical-abstractions.txt:379:- Capture mainline Megaplan behavior with normalized golden fixtures for fresh planning, gate iteration, tiebreaker, human/suspension if available, finalize/execute/review, and resume-sensitive paths.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-02-technical-abstractions.txt:381:- Define `WorkflowManifest` v1 dataclasses/serialization and core validation for nodes, refs, edges, policies, source spans, capabilities, budgets, retry, loop, fanout, subpipeline, human gate, reentry IDs, topology hash, and manifest hash.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-02-technical-abstractions.txt:385:- Define how existing discovery/package manifests coexist with or are superseded by `WorkflowManifest` v1. Package discovery manifests are not runtime manifests, but the plan must state whether they survive as package metadata and how trust gates map to workflow manifests.
