docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-02-technical-abstractions.txt:406:- Generic suspension is a runtime/kernel primitive, not a human-gate synonym. A node may be suspendable without using the human capability, and a human-capable node need not suspend.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-02-technical-abstractions.txt:490:The reviewer should be able to build a minimal Megaplan-shaped explicit-node pipeline, compile it to a serializable manifest, inspect it as YAML/DOT/dry-run data, and see compile-time rejection of non-durable Python identities.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-02-technical-abstractions.txt:497:- Create `arnold/patterns` constructors for `agent`, `branch`, `critique`, `fanout`, `human_gate`, `loop`, `merge`, `panel`, `retry`, `review`, `revise`, `subpipeline`, `tournament`, and `external_call` as pure serializable/lowerable values.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-02-technical-abstractions.txt:501:- Lower branch, loop, fanout, retry, human gate, and subpipeline shapes to manifest scopes and `reentry_id`s.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-02-technical-abstractions.txt:522:- Runtime branching uses `branch`, `loop`, `fanout`, `retry`, `subpipeline`, and `human_gate`, not Python `if`/`while` over runtime refs.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-02-technical-abstractions.txt:547:2. Pattern lowering tests cover branch, loop, fanout, retry, human gate, subpipeline, merge, and external call.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-02-technical-abstractions.txt:590:The reviewer should be able to run fake-backend workflows for linear, branch, loop, fanout, retry, subpipeline, human gate, resume, and replay scenarios without executing Python object graphs or native generator frames.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-02-technical-abstractions.txt:603:- Resolve capabilities and effects through neutral string-keyed registries/contracts. Product packages may register policy-specific handlers, but the runner must not import product policy classes, prompt templates, gate literals, or Megaplan override logic.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave3/w3-02-technical-abstractions.txt:604:- Implement generic suspension as a first-class runtime terminal state and resume path. Human gates are one product-facing use of suspension, not the runtime definition of suspension.
