docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave1/w1-09-conformance.txt:3:The conformance gates in expectation 9 are well-intentioned but miss critical dimensions while leaving several existing gates too vague to be machine-enforceable. The current list is **too broad** (terms like "import graph checks" and "behavior goldens" lack precise scope) and **missing** key gates: type-check/stub conformance, console entrypoint verification, package metadata validation, cross-branch contamination checks, import-error quality gates, and live-execution parity (not just golden parity).
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave1/w1-09-conformance.txt:11:| A | **Type-check / `py.typed` gate** | Import greps can't detect re-exports or stale `__all__` entries. A `mypy`/`pyright` clean pass on the public surface proves no old types leak. |
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave1/w1-09-conformance.txt:12:| B | **Console entrypoint removal gate** | M6 mentions deleting entrypoints but provides no machine check. Must grep `pyproject.toml` `[project.scripts]` and installed `bin/` for old command names. |
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave1/w1-09-conformance.txt:13:| C | **Package metadata gate** | `pyproject.toml` package discovery, `packages`, and `[tool.setuptools]` must not list deleted packages. No milestone checks this. |
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave1/w1-09-conformance.txt:14:| D | **Import-error quality gate** | M6 Done Criteria #1 checks `import megaplan` fails, but a bare `ModuleNotFoundError` is ambiguous. The gate must verify it raises a **specific** migration error with a migration path message. |
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave1/w1-09-conformance.txt:15:| E | **Cross-branch contamination gate** | After M6 merges, a gate must verify `origin/main` doesn't reintroduce deleted surfaces from merge artifacts or stale branches. Currently untested. |
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave1/w1-09-conformance.txt:16:| F | **Live-execution parity gate** | Golden fixtures cover static output but not live runtime with real backends. At minimum, one live-backed smoke path (even with a cheap model) must pass before M6 deletion. |
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave1/w1-09-conformance.txt:35:- **M6**: Add Gate E (cross-branch contamination) as the final gate, running the full forbidden-import and deletion-gate suite against the merged result, not just the feature branch.
docs/arnold/workflow-manifest-runtime-review/subagent-results/wave1/w1-09-conformance.txt:41:1. **M6 final gate suite must pass against the merge commit**, not the feature branch.
