arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/instructions.md:24:All other flags (`--robustness`, `--auto-approve`, `--phase-model`, `--hermes`, subagent mode, overrides, step editing) behave identically in both modes. The workflow phases are the same: `prep → plan → critique → gate → revise → finalize → execute → review`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/instructions.md:71:5. `revise` when gate recommends iteration
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/instructions.md:77:At `--robustness light`, the loop is: `plan` → `critique` → `revise` → `finalize` → `execute`. There is no prep, no gate, and no review.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/instructions.md:86:- `revise`: show the delta, flags addressed, and flags remaining. At light robustness, routes to `finalize`; otherwise loops back through `critique` and `gate`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/instructions.md:87:- `review`: judge success against the success criteria and the user's intent, not plan elegance. Only block on `must` criteria failures. `should` failures are flagged but don't require rework. `info` criteria are waived.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/instructions.md:125:Use `replan` when the orchestrator itself needs to edit the plan directly instead of asking the revise worker to do it.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/instructions.md:154:File format: TOML with a `[profiles.<name>]` table. Keys are phase names (`plan`, `prep`, `critique`, `revise`, `gate`, `finalize`, `execute`, `loop_plan`, `loop_execute`, `review`, `tiebreaker_researcher`, `tiebreaker_challenger`); values are agent specs like `"claude"`, `"codex"`, `"hermes:fireworks:accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p6"`, `"hermes:glm-5.1"`. Example:
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/instructions.md:257:`<launcher> feedback --plan <name>` scaffolds a `feedback.md` file in the plan directory and opens it in `$EDITOR` (or `$VISUAL`). The file has one section per workflow stage — `prep`, `plan`, `critique`, `revise`, `gate`, `tiebreaker`, `finalize`, `execute`, `review` — plus an `Overall` section. Each section has a `rating:` (integer 0–10) and a free-form `comment:` field; leave any field blank to skip it.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/instructions.md:302:<launcher> revise --plan <name>
