arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:75:- Treat all notes as context. If the newest note changes direction, treat that note as the new intent and decide whether to continue, revise, replan, or break out.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:87:- `init -> prep -> plan -> critique -> revise -> finalize -> execute -> done`
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:91:- After the light `revise`, the CLI moves to `gated`, so the next command is `finalize`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:101:- If `review` returns `needs_rework`, the workflow becomes `finalized -> execute -> review` again until review passes or the CLI reaches its cap.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:117:  Trigger: the latest gate recommendation is `ITERATE`, so `valid_next` includes `revise` but not `override force-proceed`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:118:  Action: run `<launcher> revise --plan <name>`, then continue back through `critique` and `gate`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:123:  Trigger: the latest gate recommendation is `PROCEED`, but preflight still blocked execution, so state stays `critiqued` and `valid_next` offers `revise` plus `override force-proceed`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:124:  Action: do not finalize yet. Use `orchestrator_guidance` plus `preflight_results` to fix the blocking checks through `revise`. On iteration 1, the guidance text may stay generic, so inspect `preflight_results` yourself before revising. If the blocker cannot be resolved safely without a user decision, stop with `BREAKPOINT: GATE_BLOCKED`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:131:- If `review` returns `needs_rework`, the CLI moves back to `finalized` with `next_step` set to `execute`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:133:- This rework loop is capped by the CLI at {max_review_rework_cycles} `needs_rework` cycles. If the cap is hit, the CLI force-proceeds to done and records the issue.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:149:  `Score improving (<previous> -> <current>). Continue to revise.`
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:170:  Trigger: you are in the `gate_proceed_blocked` branch and need the outer user to decide between more revision and `override force-proceed`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:176:  Trigger: `execute` reaches the no-progress cap, or repeated blocking/timeouts prevent forward progress.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:187:- If you hit {max_execute_no_progress} consecutive `execute` attempts without forward progress, stop with `BREAKPOINT: EXECUTE_ESCALATE`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:188:- If `execute` times out or is blocked, retry up to that same {max_execute_no_progress}-attempt cap.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:192:- If `review` returns `needs_rework`, do not break out. Follow the rework loop and run `execute` again from `finalized`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:244:- `<launcher> override replan` is available from `critiqued`, `gated`, or `finalized`. Use it when the orchestrator itself needs to edit the plan directly instead of asking the revise worker to do it.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:275:- `<launcher> revise --plan <name>`
