     1	# Megaplan Native Semantic Parity Corrective Master Plan
     2	
     3	Generated: 2026-07-09
     4	
     5	This is a corrective execution plan, not an implementation report. It treats
     6	`docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-conformance-report.md` as a
     7	historical false pass and makes closure depend on source-derived semantic
     8	evidence, not path existence, topology hashes, compatibility projections, or
     9	manual tables.
    10	
    11	Outcome target: the product of this plan should make
    12	`arnold_pipelines/megaplan/workflows/workflow.pypeline` and its imported named
    13	native subworkflows match the semantic shape described by
    14	`docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-report.md`, but with one important
    15	qualification: the representation report is target history, not proof. The final
    16	source should expose the same report-owned branches, loops, fanouts, joins,
    17	caps, route labels, policies, and phase boundaries from source, while final
    18	status is proven by strict checker evidence, carrier-scan reconciliation,
    19	split-outcome baselines, and mutation gates.
    20	
    21	Execution posture: use the hybrid lean plan. The goal is not to build a
    22	self-defending governance system around the migration; the goal is to make false
    23	semantic closure impossible while keeping the implementation focused on the
    24	North Star. Controls that directly block the historical false-pass pattern stay
    25	programmatic. Controls that mostly replace human attention become sprint review
    26	questions, adversarial audit prompts, or halt-and-ask triggers.
    27	
    28	Core controls that remain programmatic:
    29	
    30	- The row registry must be complete. A structural carrier scan is authoritative
    31	  for discovering route-authoritative hidden semantic carriers, and every such
    32	  carrier maps to a row ID, is removed, or is explicitly fenced as inert
    33	  compatibility. S7 fails on unmapped route-authoritative carriers.
    34	- Golden split-outcome baselines are captured before extraction while the old
    35	  path is still authoritative. Later parity and mutation gates compare against
    36	  those frozen baselines.
    37	- Rejection rules are structural for prohibited route authority, not token/name
    38	  blacklists. They must catch the real forbidden classes: `handler_ref`,
    39	  `route_bindings`, component route authority, manifest/backend route
    40	  translation, auto next-step derivation, CLI dispatch, and compatibility
    41	  projection evidence.
    42	- Feature flags are temporary rollout scaffolding only. No sprint closes with
    43	  dual route authority alive; rollback is by reverting the sprint.
    44	- A current-shape negative fixture is permanent CI and pinned to diagnostic
    45	  codes. Renamed/re-encoded adversarial fixtures are kept as a focused suite, not
    46	  expanded into a fixture treadmill for every new spelling of a carrier.
    47	- Baselines must be produced by a deterministic replay harness with hash-pinned
    48	  canned worker payloads. Live model output is not admissible as a golden oracle.
    49	- Baseline rewrites and route-authoritative exemptions are halt-and-ask events:
    50	  they require a short reviewed record, but not a broad governance subsystem.
    51	- Row-registry exemptions are bounded for route-authoritative carriers. S7 fails
    52	  if any scheduled route-authoritative exemption remains open.
    53	- The manifest backend remains an execution substrate for lowered source, but is
    54	  quarantined as semantic evidence. "Quarantine" means it cannot prove source
    55	  authority, not that the existing DSL/manifest runtime must be deleted in this
    56	  epic.
    57	- Dynamic `parallel_map` is not assumed to work merely because the compiler
    58	  preserves `FanoutPolicy(mode="dynamic")`. S1b must prove runtime support for
    59	  dynamic `items_ref` fanout, suspension/reentry, and loop exit semantics before
    60	  extraction sprints rely on those constructs.
    61	- Golden baselines default to route/state/next-command/suspension assertions.
    62	  Canonicalized artifact hashes are added only when artifact content is used as
    63	  parity proof; raw hashes with timestamps, UUIDs, absolute paths, invocation ids,
    64	  or worker session ids are never admissible.
    65	- Headless split-outcome gates require an explicit control-injection API. A
    66	  scenario that can only be driven through an interactive CLI is not CI evidence,
    67	  but the API should cover only required split outcomes such as approval,
    68	  resume-clarify, and tiebreaker decisions.
    69	- Topology-changing sprints require a serialized-plan decision. If live suspended
    70	  plans must survive, add migration fixtures; otherwise document and enforce a
    71	  drain/quarantine window before rollout.
    72	- Carrier scan reconciliation is tiered. Route-authoritative carriers block
    73	  closeout unless mapped or removed; descriptive metadata must be classified and
    74	  reviewable so exemption volume cannot hide live route authority.
    75	- Installed-package mode must load `.pypeline` source through package resources
    76	  from the installed artifact, not through checkout-relative paths. Run this as
    77	  an S1 smoke and an S7 final gate, plus any sprint that changes packaging.
    78	
    79	Controls downgraded from mandatory infrastructure:
    80	
    81	- Full worker/model I/O replay is not part of the base plan. Route/state replay
    82	  with canned payloads is sufficient for this end-state unless a later sprint
    83	  chooses artifact-level parity proof that needs deeper interception.
    84	- Mutation evidence is plain behavior tests and dead-delete tests, not a separate
    85	  mutation-artifact framework.
    86	- Full package-wide carrier scans run in S1 and S7. Per-sprint scans are targeted
    87	  to changed files plus a North Star review question about newly introduced route
    88	  authority.
    89	- Baseline amendment and exemption ledgers are simple reviewed records, not
    90	  autonomous governance machinery.
    91	
    92	Escalate back to the full apparatus if any sprint passes while a
    93	route-authoritative carrier remains unmapped, a checker bypass is used for
    94	closeout, a renamed/re-encoded carrier evades the focused structural suite,
    95	deterministic scenarios flake or require baseline regeneration, old carriers
    96	still affect behavior after dead-delete tests, installed-package behavior diverges
    97	at S7, or live suspended plans must survive topology-changing rollout.
    98	
    99	## 1. Ground-Truth Status
   100	
   101	The required DeepSeek gate passed. I launched one smoke test with:
   102	
