   144	`PYENV_VERSION=3.11.11 pytest tests/arnold/workflow/test_row_evidence_checker.py -q` passed: `25 passed in 0.05s`.
   145	
   146	Discrepancies vs prior reports:
   147	
   148	- The false conformance report lists all 31 rows as implemented (`docs/arnold/megaplan-native-representation-conformance-report.md:26-56`), but strict source checking fails current canonical source with 9 `AWF245` diagnostics.
   149	- The repository has a closure bypass: `check_workflow_file` defaults `evidence=None` (`arnold/workflow/source_compiler.py:623-638`), while `check_workflow_source` defaults strict `evidence=()` (`arnold/workflow/source_compiler.py:642-649`). `check_workflow_source` only calls `_row_evidence_diagnostics` when `evidence is not None` (`arnold/workflow/source_compiler.py:687-690`).
   150	- Current CLI source commands route through `check_workflow_file(source_path)` without evidence in `arnold/cli/workflow.py:207-208`, `:433-438`, `:513-515`, and `:676-677`, so they do not enforce AWF245.
   151	- The mission referred to `workflows/_compatibility.py`; the repo path is `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/_compatibility.py`.
   152	
   153	Remaining semantic carriers verified in current source:
   154	
   155	- `workflow.pypeline` imports `AUTHORING_*` and child workflow constants from `components.py` (`workflow.pypeline:14-34`), declares `handler_ref` and `route_bindings` in canonical source (`workflow.pypeline:81-280`), and declares route-heavy topology contracts (`workflow.pypeline:281-383`).
   156	- `planning.py` still merges lowered source with component metadata and route bindings: `_route_id_for_lowered_route` consults declared/component `route_bindings` (`planning.py:247-268`), `_metadata_for_step` preserves `handler_ref`, `policy_refs`, and `override_actions` (`planning.py:583-598`), and `build_pipeline()` still builds canonical DSL steps/routes from component-backed structures (`planning.py:695-716`).
   157	- `components.py` contains policy surfaces that are route tables in disguise: gate route groups and reprompt policy (`components.py:1154-1237`), revise termination/reentry policy (`components.py:1239-1336`), tiebreaker decision routes (`components.py:1392-1399`, `:2546-2550`), execute fanout/retry/route surfaces (`components.py:1694-1781`), review reducer routes (`components.py:2664-2669`), and override dispatch surfaces (`components.py:399-433`, `:1603-1621`).
   158	- `_compatibility.py` projects DSL routes into a `NativeProgram` (`arnold_pipelines/megaplan/_compatibility.py:101-115`, `:173-207`) and can run phases through CLI `COMMAND_HANDLERS` (`_compatibility.py:235-267`).
   159	- The manifest backend remains a route brain: it maps handler response fields to branch edge ids (`runtime/manifest_backend.py:227-322`) and imports component route bindings for `route_signal` resolution (`runtime/manifest_backend.py:173-189`).
   160	- `route_dispatch.py` falls back to component route bindings outside front-half lowered routes (`arnold_pipelines/megaplan/route_dispatch.py:26-43`).
   161	- Handler/execute state mutation still exists in `handlers/execute.py`, `handlers/finalize.py`, `handlers/gate.py`, `handlers/override.py`, `handlers/plan.py`, `handlers/review.py`, `execute/batch.py`, and `execute/step_edit.py` by AST scan for `current_state`, `next_step`, and `resume_cursor`.
   162	- The historical handler purity inventory still classifies 9 of 11 Megaplan handlers as report-semantic owners and 2 as pure phase bodies (`docs/arnold/megaplan-composition-conformance-report.md:74-88`).
   163	
   164	Runtime narrowing: this plan delivers source-authoritative `.pypeline` lowered into the existing DSL/manifest runtime. It does not deliver the full ordinary-async-Python resumable runtime described in `.megaplan/initiatives/legacy-loose-briefs/research/native-python-runtime-full-spec-codex.md:5-16` or the final ordinary-Python example in `.megaplan/initiatives/native-python-pipelines/research/native-python-pipelines-end-goal-megaplan-example.md:3-10`. Any closeout artifact that claims full ordinary async Python runtime parity fails S1/S7.
   165	
   166	## 2. Verified Subagent Synthesis
   167	
   168	Five DeepSeek audits completed successfully. I spot-checked their claims against source and used only claims with file:line support.
   169	
   170	- SA1 found the closure bypass: `check_workflow_file` can skip row evidence, and the CLI uses it. Verified at `source_compiler.py:623-690` and `arnold/cli/workflow.py:207-208`, `:433-438`, `:513-515`, `:676-677`.
   171	- SA1 also found that S5 review/finalize rows are not in `_row_evidence_diagnostics`; `_row_evidence_diagnostics` calls `_implemented_front_half_rows` (`source_compiler.py:722-726`), while S5 rows live in `_implemented_s5_boundary_rows` (`source_compiler.py:1783-1868`). S5 currently passes on policy-surface existence checks such as `Mapping` values on `REVIEW_POLICY`/`FINALIZE_POLICY` (`source_compiler.py:1189-1220`, `:1812-1868`).
   172	- SA2 found front-half semantics concentrated in `handlers/gate.py` and `components.py`. Verified examples: debt recording in `handlers/gate.py:77-133`, no-progress tracking and termination in `handlers/gate.py:414-677`, reprompt/downgrade in `handlers/gate.py:993-1097`, gate route groups in `components.py:1154-1158`, and revise reentries in `components.py:1276-1279`.
   173	- SA3 found tiebreaker source is still a mix of child workflow metadata and state reset. Verified tiebreaker topology/decision routes in `workflow.pypeline:281-300` and `components.py:2546-2550`; replan state clearing in `arnold_pipelines/megaplan/replan_state.py:1-38`.
   174	- SA3 found execute route semantics still owned by execute handlers/policy: approval gate in `handlers/execute.py:322-345`, approval policy in `execute/policy.py:311-357`, fresh-session force in `handlers/execute.py:423-445`, execute route surfaces in `components.py:1740-1781`, and batch loop semantics in `execute/batch.py`.
   175	- SA4 found review/override/auto remain route brains: review cap behavior in `handlers/review.py`, no-review terminal in `execute/policy.py:360-408` and `handlers/execute.py:562-572`, override matrix rows in `workflows/override_matrix.py:40-149`, auto phase command translation in `auto.py:1198-1245`, and auto escalation/force-proceed paths in `auto.py`.
   176	- SA5 found evidence infrastructure exists but is not sufficient: generated evidence bundle builder (`scripts/generate_native_representation_evidence.py:1607-1712`), scenario hash builder (`:1397-1604`), installed-package fingerprints (`:916-946`), handler-purity scans (`:1018-1104`), compatibility quarantine (`:1156-1191`), and dead-delete checks (`:1194-1225`). Missing pieces are current-shape negative fixture, policy-as-route-table rejection, strict checker closure authority, per-sprint mutation gates, and row-to-scenario coverage cross-check.
   177	
   178	Ten question-specific DeepSeek audits were then run with one subagent per
   179	question under `.tmp/native-semantic-parity-question-audit/`. Nine returned
   180	usable reports in the fan-out; Q1 was rerun separately because its first output
   181	was incomplete. The disagreements with the plan are:
   182	
   183	- Q1: `parallel_map` lowers to `Step(kind="parallel_map")` plus
   184	  `FanoutPolicy(mode="dynamic")`, but the neutral router only fans out from
   185	  static `width`; `items_ref` is not resolved at runtime. S1b therefore needs a
   186	  compiler/runtime substrate gate before S2-S5 depend on dynamic fanout.
   187	- Q2: worker/model invocation paths are heterogeneous; the current auto-drive
   188	  corpus replays route/state traces, not model I/O. Baselines should start as
   189	  deterministic route/state assertions unless a separate invocation interceptor
   190	  lands.
   191	- Q3: checker rejection is currently token/name-oriented and the row registry
   192	  lives in code, which confirms the need for the S1a data registry and structural
   193	  rejection work already listed here.
   194	- Q4: `handler_ref` is not required by the neutral Step/runtime protocol, but
   195	  Megaplan's manifest backend still dispatches through hard-coded node ids.
   196	  S1b must prove native phase dispatch without semantic dependence on
   197	  `handler_ref`.
   198	- Q5: replay cursors include manifest hashes; topology changes can quarantine
   199	  suspended plans without a migration or drain policy. Each topology-changing
   200	  sprint needs a pre-sprint serialized fixture resumed on post-sprint code, or a
   201	  deliberate drain/quarantine rollout decision.
   202	- Q6: no external pipeline import of Megaplan `components.py` was found, but
   203	  `arnold/workflow/source_compiler.py` contains string couplings to component
   204	  export names. S1a/S2-S6 need a cross-package coupling ledger so checker
   205	  strings move in lockstep with deleted component exports.
   206	- Q7: resume-clarify has a programmatic control path, but destructive approval
   207	  denial/approval and tiebreaker decisions do not. S1a needs headless
   208	  control-injection actions before those scenarios can be CI gates.
   209	- Q8: artifact/state outputs contain timestamps, UUIDs, absolute paths,
   210	  invocation ids, snapshot ids, and worker session ids. Baseline hash gates need
   211	  a canonicalizer and a pinned canonicalizer version.
   212	- Q9: package-wide carrier heuristics find hundreds of route-shaped candidates,
   213	  not about 30. S1a must tier carriers into route-authoritative vs descriptive
   214	  metadata before row reconciliation is realistic.
   215	- Q10: package data config appears to include `.pypeline` files, but no strict
   216	  installed-package checker path currently exists. S1a must implement it with
   217	  `importlib.resources` and a smoke test against an installed artifact.
   218	
   219	## 3. Milestone Plan
   220	

